  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Can't Hide Love**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **A Song For You**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Intro by Nigel Hall**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Move On Up**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **James Brown Medley**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Backwards Jack [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2009-04-26.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 146 min [1]\n- **soulive2009-04-26.flac16**: source not stated; 15 songs; 146 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Nigel Hall opened with a mini-set; his first song was solo on Rhodes, uncaptured, with recording starting when Alan and Neal appeared [1]\n- Lineup: Nigel Hall vocals, Alan Evans drums, Eric Krasno guitar, Neal Evans Hammond organ and clavinet, Russell Gunn trumpet on a couple tunes [1]\n- Nigel Hall opened with a mini-set; his first song was solo on Rhodes, uncaptured, with recording starting when Alan and Neal appeared [2]\n- Lineup: Nigel Hall vocals, Alan Evans drums, Eric Krasno guitar, Neal Evans Hammond organ and clavinet, Russell Gunn trumpet on a couple tunes [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2009-04-26.flac24**: taped by taperjoe; transferred by taperjoe; source: (2) AKG C-414B-ULS (cardioid, aimed at PA, 7' high) > 722 (24/96 w/ 40 Hz roll-off @ 24 dB/oct.) [1]. Also: Taperjoe recorded from front of board, DFC, about 25 feet from the stage, and transferred it; this is a 24-bit/96 kHz version [1]\n- **soulive2009-04-26.flac16**: taped by taperjoe; transferred by taperjoe; source: (2) AKG C-414B-ULS (cardioid, aimed at PA, 7' high) > 722 (24/96 w/ 40 Hz roll-off @ 24 dB/oct.) [2]. Also: Taperjoe recorded from front of board, DFC, about 25 feet from the stage, and transferred it; this is the 16-bit version [2]",
